   "daf": "52b",
   "sentenceId": 9,
   "he": "רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר אוֹמֵר: כּוּלָּם חוֹזְרִים בַּיּוֹבֵל. סָבַר לַהּ כְּרַבָּנַן דְּאָמְרִי: ״תָּשׁוּבוּ״ לְרַבּוֹת אֶת הַמַּתָּנָה, וְהָנֵי כּוּלְּהוּ מַתָּנָה נִינְהוּ. בְּכוֹר — ״לָתֶת לוֹ פִּי שְׁנַיִם״, מַתָּנָה קַרְיֵיהּ רַחֲמָנָא.",
   "en": "The mishna further teaches that «Rabbi Elazar says: All these» lands «return in the Jubilee» Year. The Gemara explains that Rabbi Elazar «holds in accordance with» the opinion of «the Rabbis, who say» that the term «“you shall return”» serves «to include a gift, and» he further maintains that «these» cases listed in the mishna «are all» considered «gifts.» The Gemara elaborates: With regard to «a firstborn» it is stated: «“By giving him a double portion.”» Through the use of the term “giving,” «the Merciful One calls» his portion «a gift.»"
  }
 ],
